+    "**Reading the spur chart.** Each line is one mixing product, coloured by suppression. The\n",
+    "**blue vertical strip is your input range** and the **gold horizontal strip is your output\n",
+    "range**; their intersection (black outline) is the **box**. The thick black line is the desired\n",
+    "1×1 product and runs corner to corner through the box.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**A product line passing through the box is an in-band spur**: for some input in your range it\n",
+    "lands in your output range, so no filter can remove it. Those lines are dashed (meets\n",
+    "`spec_dbc`) or bold red (fails) and are labelled beside the box. The purple dashed rectangle is\n",
+    "the **signal box** for a signal of width `signal_bw` at `signal_center`; products crossing it are\n",
+    "marked `*` and are the ones that hit the signal itself at that position. If no line crosses the\n",
+    "box, nothing in the table lands in your band at this LO."
+   ]
+  },
