+   "source": [
+    "## 7. Spectrum sweep at a node: absolute spur power through the whole chain\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Sections 3–6 give spur levels relative to the desired signal (dBc) at one mixer. To see **absolute\n",
+    "power in dBm at any point in a multi-device chain**, including the effect of filters and gain on\n",
+    "each spur, trace tones through the whole system: `System.trace_tones`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A swept CW source goes in. Every mixing product is followed: each device applies its own S21 at the\n",
+    "product's *actual* frequency (so filters reject spurs and amplifiers boost them) and each mixer with a\n",
+    "`spur_table` splits every incoming tone into its m×n products.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The chain below has real filter responses. Here they are synthetic band-pass filters standing in for\n",
+    "measured `.s2p` files."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 17,
+   "id": "47359665",
