+   "id": "98514d6a",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "**(b) Data coverage.** A device's S-parameters only cover the frequencies you measured or defined. A tone\n",
+    "outside that range gets the *edge value*, which is a guess, not data. Such points are drawn as **hollow\n",
+    "markers**, and the side list and tooltip name the devices. They are also in the dataset\n",
+    "(`extrapolated`, `extrap_devices`) and in `summary()`, which gives the devices involved and the\n",
+    "percentage of sweep points affected. Here the LNA and mixer were defined only over the 6 GHz band and\n",
+    "the IF amplifier only over the L-band, while the source sweeps 1-20 GHz. So the desired path is\n",
+    "flagged wherever the sweep leaves the band (its hollow markers are the arch's skirts), and most spurs\n",
+    "are flagged somewhere. The IF band-pass was built from 0.05 to 45 GHz, so it is flagged only for\n",
+    "products below 50 MHz or above 45 GHz. The in-band part of each arch is real data; the rest is a\n",
+    "guess. If a flagged spur matters, supply data that covers its frequency."
+   ]
+  },
